{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1957","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Carousel of Combinations"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an integer $$$n$$$. The function $$$C(i,k)$$$ represents the number of distinct ways you can select $$$k$$$ distinct numbers from the set {$$$1, 2, \\ldots, i$$$} and arrange them in a circle$$$^\\dagger$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the value of $$$$$$ \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n \\sum\\limits_{j=1}^i \\left( C(i,j) \\bmod j \\right). $$$$$$ Here, the operation $$$x \\bmod y$$$ denotes the remainder from dividing $$$x$$$ by $$$y$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since this value can be very large, find it modulo $$$10^9+7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\dagger$$$ In a circular arrangement, sequences are considered identical if one can be rotated to match the other. For instance, $$$[1, 2, 3]$$$ and $$$[2, 3, 1]$$$ are equivalent in a circle."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 10^5$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^6$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer on a new line — the value of the expression to be calculated modulo $$$10^9+7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n1\n3\n6\n314159\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n4\n24\n78926217\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, $$$C(1,1) \\bmod 1 = 0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$C(1,1)=1$$$ (the arrangements are: $$$[1]$$$); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$C(2,1)=2$$$ (the arrangements are: $$$[1]$$$, $$$[2]$$$); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$C(2,2)=1$$$ (the arrangements are: $$$[1, 2]$$$); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$C(3,1)=3$$$ (the arrangements are: $$$[1]$$$, $$$[2]$$$, $$$[3]$$$); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$C(3,2)=3$$$ (the arrangements are: $$$[1, 2]$$$, $$$[2, 3]$$$, $$$[3, 1]$$$); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$C(3,3)=2$$$ (the arrangements are: $$$[1, 2, 3]$$$, $$$[1, 3, 2]$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" In total, $$$\\left(C(1,1) \\bmod 1\\right) + \\left(C(2,1) \\bmod 1\\right) + \\left(C(2,2) \\bmod 2\\right) + \\left(C(3,1) \\bmod 1\\right) + \\left(C(3,2) \\bmod 2\\right) + \\left(C(3,3) \\bmod 3\\right) = 4$$$."}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1957E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1957/problem/E"}